BMW stands for Bayerische Motoren Werke (Bavarian Motor Works) and is a German multinational manufacturer of luxury vehicles and motorcycles headquartered in Munich.  Founded in 1916, the company originally produced aircraft engines during World War I before diversifying into motorcycles in the 1920s and automobiles in 1928 due to post-war restrictions. 

The BMW Group is a global premium automaker that also owns the Mini and Rolls-Royce brands, along with the BMW Motorrad motorcycle division.  Known for its driver-focused performance and the slogan "The Ultimate Driving Machine," BMW became the world’s ninth-largest vehicle producer in 2023, with a diverse lineup ranging from sedans like the 3 Series and 7 Series to SUVs like the X5 and high-performance M models.
